    "case_for": "The album is the definitive small-group realization of Russell's Lydian Chromatic Concept — the record that moved his theory from the concert-hall scores of *Jazz Workshop* into a working sextet, making it his defining statement under rubric signal 2. Session gravity is exceptional for a single 1961-05-08 Plaza Sound date: Eric Dolphy on alto and bass clarinet at the threshold of his peak period, Don Ellis before his microtonal big bands, Dave Baker, and one of Steve Swallow's earliest major recordings (obs, S1–S3). Lineage runs both directions: the radical recastings of Miles's 'Nardis' and Monk's ''Round Midnight' show the post-bop generation re-reading its immediate past, while the angular modal vocabulary points forward to Dolphy's Blue Note work and the freer small groups of the mid-60s. The rationale reports top-tier critical consensus (AllMusic 5 stars, Penguin 4 stars, Rolling Stone 5 stars), and 1961 is safely inside the post-bebop center of the canon's gravity — no opened-gate standing rules apply.",
    "case_against": "The real case against is the discovery test: Russell's arrangements are theory-forward and angular, and a listener sent to this cold may hear an intellectual exercise where a *Saxophone Colossus* or *Moanin'* delivers visceral pleasure — its canonical status among musicians and critics may outrun its accessibility. Second, the sourcing is thinner than the rationale claims: the dossier's actual source objects are database-level (AllMusic, Wikipedia, Discogs, iTunes API, MusicBrainz), and the Penguin/Rolling Stone ratings are asserted in the rationale but not captured as sources — min_sources is met on completeness, not on critical-text depth. Finally, track assignments are incomplete and bonus-take provenance is 'inf,' minor hygiene flags that don't bear on merit but show the dossier isn't fully load-bearing.",
    "disagreement": null,
    "recommendation": "The council proposes John treat Ezz-thetics as a core inclusion candidate — Russell's defining small-group record with an unassailable personnel network — while noting that only one reference voice argued the case, so he may wish to spot-check the discovery-test concern by listening before ruling.",
